  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/beautiful_pachytriton_arrived__en/",
      "html": "<p>The Paddletail Newts of the genus Pachytriton are available only a few weeks per year. The systematics of this genus are very confusing, so the specimens cannot be determined exactly. They are listed as Pachytriton cf. labiatus.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/beautiful_pachytriton_arrived__en/",
      "html": "<p>The tank should be quite spacious.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/beautiful_pachytriton_arrived__en/",
      "html": "<p>Pachytriton should be kept in clean water; some current is very good for the animals. No heater is needed.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/beautiful_pachytriton_arrived__en/",
      "html": "<p>Water temperature for regular keeping should be around 20°C, and 10°C during hibernation. A temporary increase of the water temperature up to 26°C does not harm the animals at all.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/beautiful_pachytriton_arrived__en/",
      "html": "<p>They feed on any type of frozen and live food that fits the mouth.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/30-amphibians-and-reptiles/beautiful_pachytriton_arrived__en/",
      "html": "<p>These newts are territorial. As in cichlids, Pachytriton give up their territorial behaviour when the population density is very high.</p><p>These newts never leave the water as long as they feel well; they are completely aquatic.</p>"
    }
  ],
